              ":answer/value": "7"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "55e253fd-ff14-5d73-82d5-cbecdabb9ef2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{7}{6}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "75015f95-cd97-50ef-af96-98a47be473bc",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "-\\frac{7}{6}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "ac414ee6-0d4d-588d-a4a0-e8547739ec11",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{11}{6}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "584bca5f-dbf0-5999-8bf5-e7143eaa38b8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{6}{7}"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "55e253fd-ff14-5d73-82d5-cbecdabb9ef2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & k & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}|)+((-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|)+((-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & k \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot ((k)\\cdot (1)-(0)\\cdot (-3)))+((-2)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (1)-(0)\\cdot (2)))+((-3)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(k)\\cdot (2)))\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot (k))+((-2)\\cdot (-1))+((-3)\\cdot (3-2k))\\\\ &=(0)+(2)+(6k-9)\\\\ &=6k-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6k-7&=0\\\\ 6k&=7\\\\ k&=\\frac{7}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=\\frac{7}{6}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
